## Flow 2: Block Building - op-node → op-reth (engine_forkchoiceUpdatedV3)

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant OpNode as op-node (Go binary)
    participant L1 as L1 Monitor
    participant HTTP as HTTP Server :9551 (JWT)
    participant EngineRPC as Engine API RPC
    participant EngineAPI as Engine API Core
    participant Consensus as Consensus Handle
    participant TreeHandler as EngineApiTreeHandler
    participant PayloadService as Payload Service
    participant PayloadBuilder as EthereumPayloadBuilder
    participant TxPool as Transaction Pool
    participant BlockBuilder as Block Builder
    participant StateRoot as State Root (TrieDB)

    Note over OpNode,StateRoot: 📍 Step 1: op-node Derives L2 Block from L1

    L1->>OpNode: Batcher transaction detected
    Note over OpNode: Decompress and decode L2 block data

    OpNode->>OpNode: Construct PayloadAttributes

    Note over OpNode,StateRoot: 📍 Step 2: op-node Calls engine_forkchoiceUpdatedV3

    OpNode->>HTTP: POST http://localhost:9551
    Note over HTTP: JWT authenticated engine_forkchoiceUpdatedV3

    HTTP->>EngineRPC: Route to engine_forkchoiceUpdatedV3
    Note over EngineRPC: File: crates/optimism/rpc/src/engine.rs L328

    EngineRPC->>EngineRPC: Validate JWT token
    EngineRPC->>EngineRPC: Parse request parameters
    Note over EngineRPC: ForkchoiceState + OpPayloadAttributes

    EngineRPC->>EngineAPI: inner.fork_choice_updated_v3_metered()
    Note over EngineAPI: File: crates/rpc/rpc-engine-api/src/engine_api.rs L396

    EngineAPI->>EngineAPI: Record metrics (start time)
    EngineAPI->>EngineAPI: Call fork_choice_updated_v3()
    Note over EngineAPI: Line 387 validate_and_execute_forkchoice()

    EngineAPI->>EngineAPI: Validate payload attributes

    EngineAPI->>Consensus: beacon_consensus.fork_choice_updated()
    Note over Consensus: File: crates/engine/primitives/src/message.rs L228

    Consensus->>Consensus: Send message to engine
    Note over Consensus: Line 243 send_fork_choice_updated()

    Note over OpNode,StateRoot: 📍 Step 3: EngineApiTreeHandler Processes Request

    Consensus->>TreeHandler: BeaconEngineMessage::ForkchoiceUpdated
    Note over TreeHandler: File: crates/engine/tree/src/tree/mod.rs L1391

    TreeHandler->>TreeHandler: Match message type

    TreeHandler->>TreeHandler: on_forkchoice_updated()
    Note over TreeHandler: Line 1019 on_forkchoice_updated()

    rect rgb(255, 240, 200)
        Note over TreeHandler: Forkchoice Update Processing
        
        TreeHandler->>TreeHandler: 1. Validate forkchoice state
        Note over TreeHandler: Line 1060 validate_forkchoice_state()

        TreeHandler->>TreeHandler: 2. Check if head already canonical
        Note over TreeHandler: Line 1091 handle_canonical_head()

        TreeHandler->>TreeHandler: 3. Apply chain update if needed

        TreeHandler->>TreeHandler: 4. Record metrics
    end

    alt payload_attributes provided
        Note over OpNode,StateRoot: 📍 Step 4: Initiate Payload Building

        TreeHandler->>TreeHandler: Check attributes present

        TreeHandler->>PayloadService: spawn_payload_job(attributes)
        Note over PayloadService: File: crates/payload/builder/src/service.rs

        PayloadService->>PayloadService: Generate payload_id

        PayloadService->>PayloadBuilder: builder.try_build(build_args)
        Note over PayloadBuilder: File: crates/ethereum/payload/src/lib.rs L88

        Note over OpNode,StateRoot: 📍 Step 5: Transaction Selection

        PayloadBuilder->>PayloadBuilder: Setup EVM environment
        Note over PayloadBuilder: Line 167

        PayloadBuilder->>PayloadBuilder: Check no_tx_pool flag

        alt no_tx_pool = false (Validator mode)
            PayloadBuilder->>TxPool: best_transactions_with_attributes()
            Note over TxPool: File: crates/transaction-pool/src/pool/txpool.rs L381

            TxPool->>TxPool: Create iterator over pending pool

            TxPool-->>PayloadBuilder: Iterator ValidPoolTransaction

        else no_tx_pool = true (Sequencer mode)
            PayloadBuilder->>PayloadBuilder: Use transactions from attributes

        Note over OpNode,StateRoot: 📍 Step 6: Block Execution

        PayloadBuilder->>PayloadBuilder: Apply pre-execution changes
        Note over PayloadBuilder: Line 195

        loop For each transaction
            PayloadBuilder->>BlockBuilder: Execute transaction
            Note over BlockBuilder: File: crates/evm/evm/src/execute.rs L515

            BlockBuilder->>BlockBuilder: Prepare transaction

            BlockBuilder->>BlockBuilder: Execute in EVM

            BlockBuilder->>BlockBuilder: Collect state changes

            BlockBuilder->>BlockBuilder: Generate receipt

            BlockBuilder-->>PayloadBuilder: gas_used and receipt

            PayloadBuilder->>PayloadBuilder: Update cumulative totals
            Note over PayloadBuilder: cumulative_gas_used += gas_usedtotal_fees += gas_price * gas_used

            alt Gas limit reached OR deadline OR cancellation
                PayloadBuilder->>PayloadBuilder: Stop transaction selection
            end
        end

        Note over OpNode,StateRoot: 📍 Step 7: State Root Calculation (TrieDB!)

        PayloadBuilder->>BlockBuilder: Finalize block
        Note over BlockBuilder: Apply post-execution changesCollect final BundleState

        BlockBuilder->>StateRoot: state_root_with_updates_triedb()
        Note over StateRoot: File: crates/storage/provider/src/providers/state/latest.rsLine: ~109Function: state_root_with_updates_triedb()


        BlockBuilder->>StateRoot: state_root_with_updates_triedb()
        Note over StateRoot: File: crates/storage/provider/src/providers/state/latest.rs L109
            Note over StateRoot: Flatten state changes to plain format

            StateRoot->>StateRoot: 2. Convert PlainPostState → HashedPostState
            Note over StateRoot: Hash all addresses and storage keys

            StateRoot->>StateRoot: 3. Load account keysto PlainPostState

            StateRoot->>StateRoot: 2. Convert PlainPostState to HashedPostState

            StateRoot->>StateRoot: 3. Load account keys

            StateRoot->>StateRoot: 4. Load storage keys

            StateRoot->>StateRoot: 5. Create TrieDB provider

            StateRoot->>StateRoot: 6. Calculate state root
            Note over StateRoot: TrieDB calculates Merkle root (342ms vs 952ms MDBX, 2.8x faster!)

            StateRoot->>StateRoot: 7. Collect trie updates

        PayloadBuilder->>PayloadBuilder: Construct ExecutionPayload
        Note over PayloadBuilder: Line: ~300ExecutionPayload {  parent_hash,  fee_recipient,  state_root,  ← TrieDB!  receipts_root,  logs_bloom,  prev_randao,  block_number,  gas_limit,  gas_used,  timestamp,  extra_data,  base_fee_per_gas,  block_hash,  ← Computed  transactions,  withdrawals,  ...}

        PayloadBuilder->>PayloadBuilder: Calculate block_hash
        Note over PayloadBuilder: Keccak256(RLP(ExecutionPayload))

        PayloadBuilder-->>PayloadService: BuildOutcome::Better(payload)
state_root and trie_updates
        BlockBuilder-->>PayloadBuilder: ExecutionOutcome

        Note over OpNode,StateRoot: 📍 Step 8: Build Execution Payload

        PayloadBuilder->>PayloadBuilder: Construct ExecutionPayload
        Note over PayloadBuilder: Includes state_root from TrieDB

        PayloadBuilder->>PayloadBuilder: Calculate block_hash
        Note over EngineAPI: latency.fork_choice_updated_v3.record()

        EngineAPI-->>EngineRPC: ForkchoiceUpdated {  payload_status: {    status: "VALID",    latest_valid_hash: "0xabc..."  },  payload_id: "0x0123..."}

        EngineRPC-->>HTTP: JSON-RPC Response

        PayloadService-->>TreeHandler: with OnForkChoiceUpdated

        EngineAPI->>EngineAPI: Record metrics (end time)

        EngineAPI-->>EngineRPC: ForkchoiceUpdated with payload_id

        EngineRPC-->>HTTP: JSON-RPC Response
        HTTP-->>OpNode: Response with payload_id

        Note over OpNode: Received payload_id, c
``` 
